{"topicSections":[{"title":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/!=(_:_:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Operators"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Equatable Implementations","role":"collectionGroup"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied\/equatable-implementations"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/Equatable-Implementations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displayed in the music notation.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLMetronome","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/BeatUnitTied/!=(_:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied\/!=(_:_:)","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"!=","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"!=(_:_:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/!=(_:_:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/BeatUnitTied":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BeatUnitTied","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The beat-unit-tied type indicates a beat-unit within a metronome mark that is tied to the preceding beat-unit."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This allows two or more tied notes to be associated with a per-minute value in a metronome mark, whereas the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome-tied element is restricted to metric relationship marks."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BeatUnitTied","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLMetronome.BeatUnitTied"}}}